这个比喻一点也不坏。这就是情况。但伯克·特伦德和泰德·希斯不知道的是，此时此刻，一个新的因素即将加入这个方程。现在，有一个我们其实没有怎么谈论过的组织，可能会让一些听众感到惊讶，那就是爱尔兰共和军，简称爱尔兰共和军。原因在于，正如我们之前所讨论的，他们曾在1962年失败了一场边境战役。爱尔兰共和军的领导层放弃了游击暴力。他们穿上高领毛衣，转向了某种马克思主义，开始和学者们混在一起。他们思考，你知道的，他们认为这个运动的未来

21
00:13:23.000 --> 00:14:04.000
of this movement is a workers' alliance to beat capitalism as well as imperialism. And that meant that during all the disturbances in 1969 that we talked about last time, the IRA are actually quite quiet. And graffiti went up in Belfast that summer. IRA equals I ran away. Now, if you're an older IRA man, if you've been active in that guerrilla movement, since, let's say, the 1940s even longer, you are very embarrassed by this. In fact, you're positively furious. So these older IRA veterans, often they're kind of cultural conservatives, very strongly Catholic. They don't have any truck with the Marxism and whatnot.
是一个工人联盟，以击败资本主义和帝国主义。这意味着在我们在上一期节目中谈到的1969年的所有骚乱期间，爱尔兰共和军其实相当安静。那年夏天，贝尔法斯特出现了涂鸦：爱尔兰共和军等于我逃跑了（IRA = I ran away）。现在，如果你是一个老资格的爱尔兰共和军成员，如果你自40年代甚至更早以来一直活跃在那个游击运动中，你对此会感到非常尴尬。事实上，你简直怒不可遏。所以这些老一代的爱尔兰共和军老兵，通常他们是某种文化保守派，天主教色彩非常浓厚。他们根本不理会马克思主义之类乱七八糟的东西。

22
00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:39.000
They're really fed up with this. They're like, why are we not getting stuck in? And then the other group, who I think are really important, are the younger militants, often in their late teens, early 20s, people who've seen action in the street fight. in Belfast and Derry in 1969. And they similarly think the IRA has basically vacated its historic role as the defender of the Catholic people of Northern Ireland. Someone should take up arms to defend our people against the loyalists and the IUC and all of this. And this comes to a head in December 1969.
他们对此真的厌烦透顶。他们会想，我们为什么不卷入其中呢？然后是另一个我认为非常重要的群体，那就是年轻的激进分子，通常处于二十岁左右的晚期，即那些在1969年的贝尔法斯特和德里街头战斗中亲历过战火的人。他们同样认为，爱尔兰共和军基本上放弃了其作为北爱尔兰天主教人民保卫者的历史角色。应该有人拿起武器来保卫我们的人民，对抗保皇党、IUC和这一切。这在1969年12月达到了一个高潮。

23
00:14:39.000 --> 00:15:10.000
There's a secret meeting of disaffected IRA men in Belfast. And they agree that they were split from the Marxist leadership. and they will set up their own rival IRA executive and army council, as they're called. And they call themselves the provisional IRA, partly to echo the text of the proclamation in the Easter rising of 1916, which had set up a provisional government of Ireland. And what happens to the original IRA? Were they still hang around? They have the official IRA.
贝尔法斯特的不满的爱尔兰共和军成员举行了一次秘密会议。他们同意脱离马克思主义领导层，建立他们自己的对手爱尔兰共和军执行委员会和军队委员会（他们是这样称呼的）。他们自称为“临时派爱尔兰共和军”，部分是为了呼应1969年复活节起义宣言的文本，该宣言曾建立了一个爱尔兰临时政府。原来的爱尔兰共和军怎么样了？他们还在周围闲逛吗？他们有“正式派爱尔兰共和军”。

24
00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:25.000
And are they still a going concern today? They effectively wound up their operations in the early 1970s. But they are still active in the period of this series. Right. So they have gunmen. They have weapons. They have seminars. Yeah.
他们今天还在运作吗？他们在20世纪70年代初实际上结束了他们的行动。但他们在这一系列事件的时期仍然很活跃。对吧。所以他们有枪手。他们有武器。他们有研讨会。是的。

25
00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:41.000
Well, they become radicalized to try and compete with the provisionals, actually. So they sort of take up the gun as well. But they end up merging, do they? Basically. No, they don't merge. I mean, there's also the INLA, which we don't need to get into them. You know, this is the nature of paramilitary groups. They tend to splinter.
嗯，他们实际上变得激进化了，试图与临时派竞争。所以他们也拿起了枪。但他们最终合并了吗？基本上。不，他们没有合并。我的意思是，还有INLA（爱尔兰国家解放军），我们不需要深入探讨他们。你知道，这就是准军事组织的性质。它们往往会分裂。

26
00:15:41.000 --> 00:16:23.000
Yeah, of course. So 10 days after this, so the. provisional IRA issued their first public statements. And they said, we're going to defend our people in the north. We're going to fight for the full political freedom of Ireland. And then early January, 1970, the political wing of the IRA, so it had always had this allied political party called Sinn Féin, that split into official and provisional factions on the same lines. And of course, as anyone who remembers the 1970s natism will know, it is the provisional IRA, the provos, that they are the people who dominate the headlines in Britain and in Ireland in the next
嗯，当然。所以在这之后的10天里，临时派爱尔兰共和军发表了他们的第一份公开声明。他们说，我们要保卫我们在北方的同胞。我们要为爱尔兰的完全政治自由而战。然后是1970年1月上旬，爱尔兰共和军的政治翼，因为它一直有一个名为新芬党（Sinn Féin）的盟友政党，该党沿着同样的路线分裂成了官方派和临时派。当然，正如任何熟悉20世纪70年代新闻的人所知，正是临时派爱尔兰共和军（即“普罗沃斯”），在接下来的大约30年里，他们成为了主导英国和爱尔兰头条新闻的人。

27
00:16:23.000 --> 00:17:10.000
30 years or so. So just to talk about them, because they are the group that everyone knows as the IRA. A couple of really important points. Sometimes when you're reading about them, you will see people say, well, they were basically set up as a defensive organisation. They were set up to defend Catholic communities from attacks by Protestant mobs in 1969. And that's where the provisional came from. This is really just not true at all. So almost all of the original leaders of the provisionals. We'll talk about them a bit later, but a guy called Sean McSiefen, Ruria Brady, Davy O'Connell, Billy McKee. These are long-standing IRA men. These are people who have been in the IRA for 10, 20, 30 years. A lot of them have served time in prison, in Britain or in Ireland.
所以，来谈谈他们吧，因为他们是每个人都知道的那个爱尔兰共和军。有几个非常重要的点。有时候当你阅读关于他们的资料时，你会看到有人说，好吧，他们基本上是作为一个防御组织建立的。他们是为了在1969年保卫天主教社区免受新教暴徒的袭击而成立的。临时派就是这么来的。这其实根本不是真的。因此，临时派几乎所有的最初领导人——我们稍后会讨论他们，但有一个叫肖恩·麦克斯特芬（Sean Mac Stiofáin）、鲁里·布雷迪（Ruairí Ó Brádaigh）、戴维·奥康奈尔（Davy O'Connell）、比利·麦基（Billy McKee）的人——都是资深的爱尔兰共和军成员。这些人已经在爱尔兰共和军待了10年、20年、30年。他们中的许多人曾在英国或爱尔兰的监狱里服刑。这些都是深信利用武力来获得一个统一的爱尔兰的准军事人员。现在，与爱尔兰共和军相关的更年轻的人也来自长期的共和党家庭。让我们看看一个人，他非常、非常坚决地否认自己曾是爱尔兰共和军的一部分。你能猜出这个人是谁吗？这难道是杰瑞·亚当斯吗？正是杰瑞·亚当斯。所以我们要记录在案，他的确否认自己加入过爱尔兰共和军。他绝对否认自己加入过爱尔兰共和军。

28
00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:44.000
These are paramilitaries who are, you know, they believe in using force to get a united Ireland. Now, even younger people associated with the IRA come from longstanding Republican families. Let's look at one person who very, very vigorously denies that he was ever part of the IRA. Can you guess who this person is? Is this Jerry Adams by any chance? It is Jerry Adams, yes. So we're just putting on the record that he does deny he was in the IRA. He absolutely denies he was in the IRA.
关于杰瑞·亚当斯，奇怪的是他否认自己加入过爱尔兰共和军，但每一位撰写相关历史的学术历史学家都相信他曾加入过。所以很难知道该相信谁，汤姆。因此，当临时派成立时，杰瑞·亚当斯21岁。杰瑞·亚当斯本人总是说：“我是通过民权运动被吸引到共和主义活动中来的。我之所以激进并加入新芬党，是因为我对保皇党的暴力感到太震惊了。”对于向美国受众传达信息时所做的架构来说，这一点很重要，不是吗？

29
00:17:44.000 --> 00:18:15.000
The strange thing about Jerry Adams is Jerry Adams denies that he was in the IRA, but every single academic historian who writes about this believes that he was. So it's hard to know who to believe there, Tom. So Jerry Adams was 21 years old when the provisionals were established. Jerry Adams himself has always said, I was drawn into Republican activism through the civil rights movement. I was radicalized to join Sinn Féin because I was so shocked by the loyalist violence. That's important, isn't it, for the framing of the message for American audiences?
因为如果你把自己塑造成站在民权运动这一边的人，我的意思是，谁会反对呢？是的，谁会不同意呢？现在，必须要说的是，杰瑞·亚当斯在这里所说的关于自己是以这种方式变得激进的话根本不是真的。杰瑞·亚当斯来自西贝尔法斯特的一个共和党家庭。他的祖父在20世纪20年代是爱尔兰共和兄弟会的成员。他的父亲是爱尔兰共和军成员。他的叔叔们也是爱尔兰共和军成员。他的父亲曾因伏击警察巡逻队而入狱。

30
00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:43.000
Because if you cast yourself as being on the side of the civil rights movement, I mean, who would object to that? Yeah, who would disagree with that? Now, it's important to say what Jerry Adams is saying here about being radicalized this way is just not true. Jerry Adams comes from a Republican family in West Belfast. His grandfather was a member of the Irish Republican Brotherhood in the 1920s. His father was in the IRA. His uncles were in the IRA. His father was jailed for an ambush on a police patrol.
所以，假设杰瑞·亚当斯说的是真的，他从来都不是爱尔兰共和军的一部分。对我和我的困惑在于他为什么不是，因为鉴于他的背景，如果他不加入才真的很奇怪，我想说。然而，你知道，世界真奇妙，不是吗？所以也许他真的没有加入。现在，另一点是关于暴力的。

31
00:18:43.000 --> 00:19:03.000
So let's assume that Jerry Adams is telling the truth, and that he was never part of the IRA. The puzzle for me is why he wasn't, because given his background, it would be very strange for him not to have joined it, I would say. However, you know, it's a funny old world, isn't it? So maybe he wasn't. Now, the other point is about violence.
与民权运动不同，临时派爱尔兰共和军对改革斯托蒙特（Stormont）政权不感兴趣。不，他们想摧毁它，不是吗？他们不想摧毁它吗？他们想要推翻斯托蒙特，他们想要赶走英国人，他们想要一个统一的爱尔兰。他们将要实现这一目标的方式

32
00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:18.000
The provisional IRA, unlike the say in the civil rights movement, are not interested in reforming the Stormont state. No, they want to destroy it, don't they? They don't want to destroy it? They want to bring down Stormont, they want to drive out the British, and they want a united Ireland. And the way that they're going to do that
就是他们委婉地称为“肉体力量”的东西。也就是暴力。他们对此完全是直言不讳的。因此，这是1970年9月的《共和党新闻》。它说：“爱尔兰人民应该认识到，英国帝国主义者不会尊重、害怕或过多关注那些为施舍或让步而乞求、卑躬屈膝或爬行的人。”换句话说，只有当你进行反击时，他们才会尊重你。

33
00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:43.000
is what they call euphemistically physical force. And that is violence. And they're completely upfront about that. So this is the Republican news in September 1970. It says, the Irish people should realize that British imperialists do not respect, fear, or pay much attention to people who beg, grovel or crawl for favours or concessions. In other words, they only respect you if you fight back.
当然，爱尔兰共和军会说——而且他们自始至终都在这样说——会有平民伤亡，但这是一场战争。这是不可避免的。这是值得的。你知道，我们会做可怕的事情，但为了得到我们想要的东西，这是值得的，目的将证明手段的正当性。这就是为什么当你进入20世纪90年代末时，老一代共和主义者常常对《耶稣受难日协议》以及爱尔兰共和军最终接受的交易感到如此被背叛。你所说的老一代共和主义者是指比他们更早一代的人吗？是的，但也包括那些自70年代以来就身在其中的人。如果你在1970年加入，对吧，你当时20岁，那么当你一切都结束时，你差不多是什么年龄？五十多岁了吧。而你生命中最美好的部分，

34
00:19:43.000 --> 00:20:28.000
Now, of course, the IRA say, and they say this throughout, there are going to be civilian casualties, but this is a war. That is inevitable. It is worth it. You know, we're going to be doing terrible things, but it is worth it to get what we want, and the end will justify the means. And that is why, when you get to the late 1990s, that is why the older Republicans often feel so betrayed by the Good Friday Agreement and the deal that the IRA ended up taking. And by the older Republicans, you mean people who are from a generation before? Yeah, but also people who've been in there since the 70s. If you joined in 1970, right, and you're 20 years old, you are what, getting into your 50s, maybe by the time it all comes to an end. And the best part of your life,
你知道的，你的黄金岁月已经过去了。你已经把那些黄金岁月用来做那些你知道是非常可怕的事情。你杀过无辜的人，但你这样做是因为你相信目的是正当的，而目的是一个统一的爱尔兰。现在你的领导人告诉你，实际上，你这么做是为了能与伊恩·佩斯利（Ian Paisley）组建联合政府并去管理供水局。而你说，什么？我的意思是，我们涉足血海。我们堕入地狱。我们基本上，你知道，为了这个出卖了我们不朽的灵魂。这就是为什么当杰瑞·亚当斯和马丁·麦吉尼斯达成交易时，人们会感到如此委屈。我的意思是，你提到了地狱和不朽的灵魂。是的。在那个语境下。我的意思是你是用隐喻吗？

35
00:20:28.000 --> 00:21:09.000
you know, your prime years are behind you. And you've, and you've, spent those prime years doing things that you know are terrible things. You have killed innocent people, but you did it because you believed the end justified the means and the end was a United Ireland. And now your leaders tell you, actually, you did it so that you could get into coalition with Ian Paisley and run the waterboard. And you say, what? I mean, we waded through blood. We descended into hell. We basically, you know, sold our immortal souls for this. And that's why people feel so aggrieved when Jerry Adams and Martin McGuinness do the deal. I mean, you mentioned hell in immortal souls. Yeah. In that. I mean, do you mean that metaphorically?
还是我们在谈论那些真正认为自己冒着失去不朽灵魂风险的人？我认为有相当多的人是非常虔诚的天主教徒。我们确切地知道，许多爱尔兰共和军成员都是虔诚的天主教徒。我的意思是，他们相信这些东西。你知道，他们生活在一个被宗教圣像包围的世界里。爱尔兰共和运动的圣像具有非常、非常、非常浓厚的天主教色彩。我想当你阅读对人们的采访，当他们回首自己的生活时，他们是在回顾自己所做的事情。

36
00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:36.000
Or are we talking about people who genuinely think that they have risked their immortal souls? I think there are quite a lot of people who are very pious Catholics. We know for a fact that a lot of IRA men were pious Catholics. I mean, they believe in this stuff. You know, they live in a world where they're surrounded by religious iconography. The iconography of the Irish Republican movement is very very, very heavily Catholic. I think when you read interviews with people, when they're looking back at their lives, they're looking about what they did.
很显然，你知道，他们沉浸在某种宗教文化中。而且我认为很多人确实觉得，你知道，我们做了可怕的事情，但我们是以更伟大的善的名义去做的。是的。你知道，我们被出卖了。我的意思是，这显然总是让人感到困惑。

37
00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:50.000
They're obviously, you know, they're steeped in a kind of religious culture. And I think a lot of people did feel, you know, we did terrible things, but we did it in the name of greater good. Yeah. You know, and we've been sold out. I mean, this is obviously always puzzles people.
为什么持续派爱尔兰共和军（Continuity IRA）或真实爱尔兰共和军（Real IRA）之类的不坐下来开会并接受《耶稣受难日协议》呢？好吧，我想这就是原因，因为他们只是感到被背叛了。不管怎样，我们话题扯得太远了。回到1970年初。所以临时派已经建立，他们的首要任务是弄到枪，而他们有强大的朋友来帮助他们做到这一点。

38
00:21:50.000 --> 00:22:10.000
Why did the continuity IRA or the real IRA or whatever? Why didn't they just get around the table and accept the Good Friday Agreement? Well, I think this is why, because they just felt betrayed. Anyway, we're jumping ahead too much. Back to early 1970. So they've been set up the provisionals, their priorities to get guns, and they have powerful friends to help them do it.
首先，他们在爱尔兰共和国有朋友。这实际上是一个非凡的故事。我认为它在英国并不是非常广为人知。1969年，爱尔兰政府拨出了10万英镑作为对被赶出北方家园的天主教家庭的救济基金。基本上至少有两名爱尔兰政府部长。因此，查尔斯·霍西（Charles Haughey，后来的爱尔兰总理，也就是首脑“T-Shook”），是的，还有一个叫尼尔·布莱尼（Neil Blaney）的人。

39
00:22:10.000 --> 00:22:38.000
So first of all, they have friends in the Republic of Ireland. This is an extraordinary story, actually. I don't think it's terribly well-known in Britain. In 1969, the Irish government had put aside £100,000 pounds as a sort of relief fund for Catholic families driven from their homes in the north. And basically at least two Irish government ministers. So Charles Hohy, later the Prime Minister of Ireland, the boss, the T-Shook, yeah, and a guy called Neil Blaney.
他们与一个曾加入党卫军（SS）的比利时商人合作使用这笔资金。他们挪用这笔资金在西德购买枪支，并将它们走私给爱尔兰共和军。这在爱尔兰共和国是一件大事。为此曾有过一场巨大的法庭诉讼。另一个地方是美国。当然，许多爱尔兰裔美国人，许多对故国有着某种，你知道的，如梦幻般记忆的爱尔兰裔美国人，对英国有一种本能的怀疑和厌恶。包括泰德·肯尼迪。包括泰德·肯尼迪。

40
00:22:38.000 --> 00:23:09.000
They collaborated with a Belgian businessman who had been in the SS to use this money. They diverted the money to buy guns in West Germany and they smuggled them to the IRA. This was a huge deal in the Republic of Ireland. There was a huge court case about it. And then the other place is America. Of course, lots of Irish Americans, lots of Irish Americans with very sort of, you know, misty-eyed memories of the old country, an instinctive suspicion and dislike of Britain. Including Ted Kennedy. Including Ted Kennedy.
你还有像诺拉黑（Noraid）这样的组织，最著名的是，他们从爱尔兰裔美国人那里筹集资金。其中很大一部分资金用于购买在加利福尼亚制造的阿玛莱特（Armalite）步枪。然后它们被走私过大西洋，令人惊奇的是，他们甚至会把阿玛莱特步枪藏在“伊丽莎白女王二号”邮轮上走私过去。哦，就像卢西塔尼亚号一样。是的，完全是这样。因此，到1970年夏天，临时派拥有了相当强大的军火库。他们有突击步枪，有半自动武器。他们有大约1000名活跃成员，这些人不仅会上街战斗，还负责经营安全屋之类的地方。他们在1970年6月底上演了宏大的登场。现在，希斯，泰德·希斯在现代英国历史上有过无与伦比的记录，我认为他做出了意图良好但灾难性的政治误判。所以他的第一次误判，这是1970年的夏天，你要禁止传统的工会游行、奥兰治秩序游行之类的事情吗？他说：“不，我不会那样做。”

